# E2E Testing

Every new or changed **App Router page** must ship with Playwright e2e tests in the same PR.

## What to Test

| Focus | Test |
|-------|------|
| Page loads | Navigate to route; assert HTTP success and key content visible |
| Primary heading | Assert main `heading` (level 1 or page title) is visible |
| Critical actions | Assert primary links, buttons, or forms render and behave correctly |
| Navigation | Assert outbound links have expected `href` or in-app navigation works |

Prefer role-based locators (`getByRole`, `getByLabel`) over CSS selectors or test IDs.

## File Placement

Add specs under `e2e/`. Name them after the route, using kebab-case and a `.spec.ts` suffix:

```
app/page.tsx                    →  e2e/home.spec.ts
app/menu/page.tsx               →  e2e/menu.spec.ts
app/orders/[id]/page.tsx        →  e2e/order-detail.spec.ts
```

One spec file per page is enough; group related scenarios in `test()` blocks within that file.

Do not put e2e specs next to page files or in `__tests__/`. The `.spec.ts` suffix in `e2e/` distinguishes Playwright specs from Vitest unit tests.

## Conventions

- Use `@playwright/test`; import `test` and `expect` from it
- Use relative paths in `page.goto()` — `baseURL` is configured in `playwright.config.ts`
- Run `npm run test:e2e` before finishing; CI runs the same command on every PR

```typescript
// e2e/menu.spec.ts
import { expect, test } from "@playwright/test";

test("menu page renders main content", async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto("/menu");

  await expect(
    page.getByRole("heading", { level: 1, name: /menu/i }),
  ).toBeVisible();
});

test("menu item links to detail page", async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto("/menu");

  const itemLink = page.getByRole("link", { name: /classic burger/i });
  await expect(itemLink).toHaveAttribute("href", "/menu/classic-burger");
});
```

## Relationship to Unit Tests

- **Pages with client components** — unit-test interactive pieces in colocated `.unit.test.tsx` files; e2e covers the full page in a real browser
- **Async Server Components** — cover with Playwright e2e, not Vitest (see unit-testing rule)
- **Layout-only route groups** with no unique page content — no e2e required for the layout itself

## Exceptions

- **Redirect-only pages** — test that the redirect target is reached
- **Auth-gated pages** — use Playwright auth fixtures or setup when added; until then, test the unauthenticated behavior explicitly
- **Minor copy or styling tweaks** — update existing e2e assertions when they break; no new spec file needed

## When Editing Existing Pages

Adding a new route segment or meaningful page behavior? Add or extend the matching e2e spec. Refactoring page structure? Update e2e assertions alongside the change.
